 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "tree is the level-order serialization used for N-ary trees: the root value, then null, then for each node in breadth-first order its children's values followed by null (trailing nulls omitted). A path [p0, ..., pL-1] matches a chain of nodes v0, ..., vL-1 where each v(i+1) is a child of v(i) and each value equals its path entry. Variant 2 (inferred follow-up): the matching chain may start at any node (it still goes downward through children); return true when one exists, else false.",
